# Fixtures are LF-canonical.
#
# Manifest expectations pin byte offsets (diagnostic spans), so the exact bytes
# matter. With core.autocrlf=true — the Windows default — a plain `*.pep` file is
# rewritten to CRLF on checkout, which shifts every offset by one byte per line
# and turns an exact span assertion into a misleading "span did not match".
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion for this directory only, so every
# checkout sees the committed LF bytes. The runner still refuses a CRLF fixture
# that pins spans (infra_error) rather than blaming the compiler.
*.pep -text
